   "name": "Heat Seeker",
   "grade": "5.10a",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Five pitches up the North East Buttress of Mt. Meeker. Cracks that are mostly continuous make the early pitches good fun; the final two are easy. Grades and lengths: 5.9 at 140ft, 5.9 at 65ft, 5.10a at 115ft, 5.7 at 125ft, 5.8 at 115ft. Pitch 1 leaves the sheer face ten feet to the right of a corner that faces left, and its first few feet resist protection. Pitch 3 holds the crux, a brief finger-width crack, after relocating the belay 50 feet along the ledge, then a traverse right. The last shares Bands and Brothers; going left avoids its unprotected offwidth.",
